    <TD align="left" valign="top" colspan="4" height="115"><b>Dellok was born under a Blessed Sign in Qeynos and was led by Rodcet Nife into a life of service to his fellow Norrathians.  He was often overheard to say to his young playmates "... I have discovered that humanity does not want to be served; on the contrary it resents any attempt to serve it." <i><font color=blue>-- Robert Heinlein Stranger in a Strange Land.</font></i><br><br>
 
Then Dellok learned how to Raise people from the dead and all that changed.<br><br>

While Dellok was freewheeling the height and breadth of Norrath, he found that he shared alot of the same interests and technique for ridding Norrath of evil as others who operated within the Guild called Protectors of Norrath. Imora, Dellok's RL partner, had already been in PoN for quite some time and so the transition was quick.  Dellok pursued many group activities in the short time he was with PoN until Aanallain facilitated his move to Warriors of Wrath, where Dellok is eager to see what contribution he can make.<br><br>

Dellok is also the father of three young maidens, 6yrs, 10yrs and 15yrs old.  They, Dellok figures, are his greatest test of Service to Rodcet Nife and so he gives them the priority of his time, but thru diligence he finds he is often able to accomodate other enteprises, such as RAIDS and meetings too. )<br><br>

So far, Dellok has stayed true to his Oath of Poverty, and despite looking for temptation he has come up empty-handed. :(<br><br>

Dellok hopes to retire on his ability to Smith Armor and Weapons and is 1 skill point from Mastery.  In the meanwhile, he continues to ply his Preaching Ways to the unholy mobs he meets, preferrably in Kunark, but occassionally just about anywhere.
</b></TD>
